 "note": "One short cue per head flash (art/concepts/marked-aura/flashes.json), each in the sound family of the fighter's shape family. Times in seconds, pitches in semitones from the family's root. A flash recipe is the same for all four fighters; the family changes only the timbre (audio/synth/flash_synth.gd). Veto rules for alert-like sounds are in docs/audio/direction.md, section 5.6. max_s is the flash's total time (attack + hold + fade): a cue is cut there with a short fade, so the sound is never longer than the flash. Hazard, Primed and Respect were added and Brink cut (EP and Orb, 2026-09-29); their times (max_s) are provisional until Art's data/art/flashes.json lands. v3: each cue is articulated to Art's pulse count (data/art/flashes.json v3: count, on, off, fade). A layer with pulsed=true swells with each pulse (a raised-cosine swell over `on`, a `floor` level between pulses, `grow` making later pulses louder), so sound and picture pulse together while a triple pulse stays one continuous sound, never a three-note alert sting. at_pulse places a layer at a pulse start. The cue is cut at the pulse total. host_check compares these numbers with Art's file.",
